- What is Color Gamut?
{sentence}
- Color Gamut is defined as the range of colors which a particular device can produce or record.
{sentence}
- It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.
{sentence}
- Commonly seen color gamut standards include NTSC, sRGB, AdobeRGB, DCI-P3, EBU, and AppleRGB.
{sentence}
- The selection of color gamut really depends on your workflow and requirements.
